  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\mathrm{I}_1=\\int_0^1 2^{x^2} d x, I_2=\\int_0^1 2^{x^3} d x, I_3=\\int_1^2 2^{x^2} d x$ and $I_4=\\int_1^2 2^{x^3} d x$ then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "HcHZg",
      "text": "\n$I_2>I_1$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2NgRq",
      "text": "\n$I_1>I_2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "5aYpF",
      "text": "\n$I_3=I_4$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dPHma",
      "text": "\n$I_3>I_4$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& l_1=\\int_0^1 2^{x^2} d x, l_2=\\int_0^1 2^{x^3} d x, I_3=\\int_0^1 2^{x^2} d x, I_4=\\int_0^1 2^{x^3} d x \\\\\n& \\forall 0 < x < 1, x^2>x^3 \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\int_0^1 2^{x^2} d x>\\int_0^1 2^{x^3} d x \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow I_1>I_2 .\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
